  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the scene of Hitler enjoying a chill day",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the ironic and satirical scene where Adolf Hitler is depicted as 'enjoying a chill day at kehlsteinhaus'. This projection is implicit, as the meme invites the viewer to imagine themselves in the context of the absurd juxtaposition — viewing Hitler through the lens of modern 'chill culture' — thereby creating a humorous or mocking perspective. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the meme (text + image) creates a direct engagement where the viewer is positioned as the one interpreting the irony, thus projecting themselves onto the scene.",
